  "briefing": "A foreign rite has found a mid-map ruin and means to complete it there; the ford watch holds the crossing below. The ground is generated fresh each time this scenario is built, so every position here is pinned to a role on that ground (the ruin, the crossing, each side's deployment zone) rather than to a fixed hex: the same scenario plays out, sensibly, whichever seed builds it. Attackers win by completing the rite; defenders win by holding the crossing for three rounds running or by surviving ten rounds."
